# PROPOSAL ONLY — audit-and-propose. Do NOT apply without owner review.
# Target (existing substrate, NOT modified by this audit):
#   https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/meta/shapes/  (.meta of the catalog container)
#
# Defect: the catalog container's dc:description cites the SUPERSEDED D77
#   ("(D77). Five shapes: page, source, person, procedure, working.")
#   while D98 (ratified 2026-05-19, supersedes D77) is the current authority and
#   the container holds 18 shape files. The "Five shapes" / D77 text is the stale
#   artifact — not the file count.
#
# Proposed replacement dc:description (apply via N3 Patch to the container .meta,
# owner-gated). Counts reconciled against D98 + the 2026-05-23 source/class-extension
# additions and the addressbook + owner-identity overlays.

@prefix dc: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/>.

<https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/meta/shapes/>
    dc:description "SHACL shape catalog. wiki-memory L3 core: 8 NodeShapes (D98, supersedes D77) — Page, Thing, Concept, Person, Place, Event, Organization, HowTo — plus WorkingNote (D73), the resource.shacl.ttl LDP guard (D38), template (L4 exemplar, D100), and the re-introduced Source via class-extension contract (D104+). Additional overlays contribute their own shapes: addressbook (contact-card, group, membership, organization-card) and owner-identity (webid-profile, pod-owner-preferences)." .

# NOTE — a SECOND, separate finding surfaced during this audit (report §3):
# overlays/wiki-memory/shapes/class-extension.shacl.ttl exists in the repo source
# but is NOT deployed to the live Pod (GET .../class-extension.shacl.ttl -> 404).
# Either it should be deployed via `make reset`, or it is intentionally repo-only.
# Resolve by owner — do NOT auto-deploy.
